%N A398622 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * H(2*k) * H(k,2) / k, where H(k) = A001008(k)/A002805(k) is the k-th harmonic number, and H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k) is the k-th harmonic number of order 2.
%H A398622 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.56, pp. 453-454, eq. (4.187), section 5.56, p. 469, section 6.56, pp. 789-794.
%H A398622 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A398622 Equals log(2)^2*zeta(2)/2 - 21*log(2)*zeta(3)/16 - 15*zeta(4)/32 - log(2)^4/8 + 2*Pi*Im(Li_3((1+i)/2)) - 3*Li_4(1/2), where i is the imaginary unit.
%e A398622 0.794850076382266026867390035949854153069163926170628...
